\begin_layout Section
Viewing and customizing the network interface
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
After having made the connection to a network we are out of the lower-level pico_cyw43_arch library and up into the pico_lwip library which contains a number of different modules but the module of relevance for viewing and customizing our network interface is NETIF.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
It is via this module that we learn all the network information that the access point gave us upon connection:
 our IP,
 netmask,
 gateway,
 etc.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In particular,
 all this information gets stored in a struct called netif_default.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This struct has three fields:
 ip_attr_t ip_addr,
 ip_addr_t netmask and ip_addr_t gw which represent the assigned IP,
 netmask and gateway.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The SDK provides some macros for viewing and modifying these network settings.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To print the fields of the global netif_default struct use the following (taken from Fairhead and James:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
printf ("IP:
 %s
\backslash
n",
 ip4addr_ntoa(netif_ip_addr(netif_default))) ;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
printf ("Mask:
 %s
\backslash
